    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d132">

                <pb facs="0498" n="323" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10-12mSupp/pg323"/>

                <head>132. Memorandum from Dungan to President Kennedy, January 22<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d132-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-01-22">January 22, 1963</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d132-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d132-1"/>
                <p>Attached are two background papers—one dealing with Haiti and one with Guatemala.
                    They were prepared for your 4 o’clock meeting today.</p>
                <p>As you will note from reading them, the situation in both countries has one
                    similarity—both regimes are discredited, there is no suitable alternative on the
                    horizon, and we have relatively few assets.</p>
                <closer><signed corresp="#p_DRA_1">Ralph A. Dungan</signed></closer>
                <pb facs="d132-2" n="2" type="facsimile" xml:id="d132-2"/>



                <xi:include href="d132-a1.xml" xpointer="d132-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d132-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d132-f1-content">
                <p>Transmits attached background paper on Guatemala. Top Secret. 3 pp. Kennedy
                    Library, President’s Office Files, Guatemala, Security, 1961–63.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
